homelab-node-exporter (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Firewall: ship /etc/nftables.d/10-homelab-metrics.nft (generated from
    /etc/homelab/node-exporter/config's MONITORING_HOSTS, default the ct19
    monitoring host) that appends an accept for this host's exporter ports
    { 8081, 8083, 8404, 9100, 9127, 9154, 9187, 9900 } to the base
    'inet filter input' chain, scoped to the monitoring host(s). The base
    input chain has a drop policy and only opens {22,53,80,443}, so nothing
    could scrape :9100 until now. Applied live via an incremental
    `add rule` (idempotent by rule comment) that never flushes the ruleset,
    so bad-ips' runtime-populated set is not disturbed; also re-applied at
    boot via nftables.conf's include. postrm purges the drop-in + live rule.

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Tue, 30 Sep 2026 13:30:00 -0500

homelab-node-exporter (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: thin fleet wrapper around the Ubuntu-archive
    prometheus-node-exporter. Depends on it (host CPU/load/mem/disk/
    filesystem/tmpfs/network metrics on :9100) and ships an
    /etc/homelab/services/node-exporter.yml manifest so homelab-agent
    advertises the exporter into the fleet topology/services view
    (kind: metrics-exporter). No config, no secrets -- deploy to every
    fleet host; the monitoring host's Prometheus scrapes each :9100.

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Tue, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0500
